==German==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|[[hōchzīt]], [[hōchgezīt]]}}, from (only plural) {{m|goh|hōhūn gizīti||high celebration}}, equivalent to {{compound|de|hoch|Zeit|t1=high|t2=time}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|de|/ˈhɔxˌt͡saɪ̯t/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Hochzeit.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Hoch|zeit}}

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[wedding]], [[marriage]] {{gloss|a ceremony in which people are married and/or a celebration thereof}}
#: {{ux|de|Die '''Hochzeit''' der Oscar-Preisträgerin war tagelang Hauptthema in der Klatschpresse.|The Oscar award winner’s '''wedding''' was the main topic of the yellow press for days.}}
# {{lb|de|card games|in [[Doppelkopf]]}} the state of having been [[deal]]t both [[queen]]s of [[clubs]]; {{ngd|used in a player’s announcement that they were dealt these and that the first player to win a non-[[trump]] [[trick]] will join their side}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich hab '''Hochzeit'''. Der erste Fehl geht mit.|I have '''both queens of clubs'''. The first non-trump joins me.}}

=====Declension=====
{{de-ndecl|f}}

